// Two three-generation blooms, a shaft to climb between two walls, embers on the crossings.
name Confluence
rule B1234/S012345678
steps 3
hint Three generations of bloom from each stone, deep in each chasm. One seed is beside you, the other on the plateau above the shaft. Embers hold the crossings; wait for them to pass.
tip Grow the first bloom to cross the chasm, climb the shaft on its blocks between the ember's passes, drop to the second stone, plant, rewind, and grow both from the far rock.
intro A river of stone with a single ford, and a shaft that climbs between two walls. On each side, a spring that bloomed for three generations. This is the last ruin, and the shape in it is one you know.
outro You planted the seeds where the springs rose, and the world grew back around you. It began here. So did you.
